{"id":"api-example-001","type":"api_behavior","fact":"Example: Prisma findMany returns an empty array [] when no records match, not null.","recommendation":"Check .length instead of checking for null/undefined.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"Prisma docs","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["prisma","database","queries"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"text":"Codex CLI writes one rollout JSONL per run at ~/.codex/sessions/<YYYY>/<MM>/<DD>/rollout-*.jsonl (codex exec runs included; rotated runs move to ~/.codex/archived_sessions/). Per-run token usage = the LAST event_msg record with payload.type=='token_count' WHOSE payload.info is non-null, then payload.info.total_token_usage {input_tokens, cached_input_tokens, output_tokens, reasoning_output_tokens}. token_count records with info:null DO occur, and a rollout can have ZERO non-null-info records (interrupted run) -> treat as unknown cost (null, never 0). Model = the LAST turn_context.payload.model (session_meta.payload.model is unreliable/null). cwd = session_meta.payload.cwd.","tags":["codex","openai","token-usage","cost","sessions-spike-v5","api-behavior"],"observed_at":"2026-05-19","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Claude Code transcript assistant records carry message.model and message.usage = {input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_creation:{ephemeral_1h_input_tokens, ephemeral_5m_input_tokens}}. The 1h and 5m cache-creation writes are priced at DIFFERENT rates — do not collapse them into one term. The record's costUSD field is null, so cost must be computed (tokens x price). Use the top-level usage.* figures, NOT usage.iterations[].","tags":["anthropic","claude","token-usage","cost","cache-pricing","sessions-spike-v5","api-behavior"],"observed_at":"2026-05-19","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"metaswarm's external-tools delegation ledger ~/.claude/sessions/external-tools.jsonl (written by emit_json/log_session in the plugin's skills/external-tools/adapters/_common.sh) has one record per delegation: {schema_version, tool, command, model, attempt, exit_code, branch, git_sha, files_changed, diff_stats, duration_seconds, cost:{input_tokens,output_tokens}, raw_log, error_type, timestamp}. `command` and `raw_log` are SECRET-BEARING — parse with a Zod schema that .pick()s only the needed fields so they are structurally dropped. The record has NO cwd, so per-project attribution from the ledger alone is not determinable. The ledger only exists once metaswarm has actually delegated — handle an absent file as empty. NOTE the plugin's own extract_cost_codex() is broken (reads a .usage key codex 0.130 no longer emits) — bead metaswarm-dashboard-d2u.","tags":["metaswarm","external-tools","ledger","gemini","secrets","sessions-spike-v5","api-behavior"],"observed_at":"2026-05-19","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
